  "metric": "AUC, the area under the ROC curve. 0.5 is chance and 1.0 is perfect.",
  "intervals": "Intervals are 95 percent percentile intervals from 2000 speaker-level bootstrap draws. Paired differences use one speaker draw per replicate for both sides.",
  "probe": "A linear probe is a logistic regression on the model's hidden states, trained and tested on speaker-disjoint folds. Its layer is chosen inside the training folds and its AUC is the mean over five fold assignments.",
